Based on my analysis, this section modifies Django's GIS database model field layer (`django/contrib/gis/db/models/fields.py`). The changes involve: (1) refactoring `get_srid`, `get_db_prep_save`, and `get_prep_value` up to `BaseSpatialField` to handle `GDALRaster`, (2) adding a `RasterField.get_transform` method that dynamically creates a `SpecificRasterBandTransform` class based on an integer band index, and (3) registering GIS lookups on `BaseSpatialField`.

This is a low-level ORM/database field layer. It performs no request handling, user identification, or access-control decisions. The `get_transform` method uses `int(name)` to validate the band index (a DoS-safe integer conversion), and `RasterBandTransform.as_sql` simply compiles the left-hand side — no user-controlled identifiers are fetched or authorization checks bypassed. The retrieved security policy excerpts concern the admin querystring lookup whitelist and the auth/permission framework, none of which apply to this database field layer. There is no CWE-639, CWE-862, or CWE-863 candidate here.

